section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Not in any embedded face. These are written as codepoints because writing them as glyphs would drop them."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: auto
  padding-top: 6pt
  gap: 14pt
  column
    width: fill
    text "CJK ideographs      U+4E00-U+9FFF"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Hangul              U+AC00-U+D7A3"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Hiragana / katakana U+3040-U+30FF"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Emoji               U+1F300-U+1FAFF"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Hebrew              U+0590-U+05FF"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Arabic              U+0600-U+06FF"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
  column
    width: fill
    text "BALLOT BOX          U+2610, U+2611, U+2612"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "BALLOT X            U+2717, HEAVY CHECK U+2714"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Geometric shapes    U+25A0-U+25FF"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Stars               U+2605, U+2606"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Double arrows       U+21D0, U+21D2, U+21E7"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt
    text "Mac modifier keys   U+2318, U+2325, U+232B"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 7pt

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Two gaps worth knowing individually:"
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: auto
  padding-top: 5pt
  text "U+2011 NON-BREAKING HYPHEN is missing from IBM Plex Mono and present in Sans and Serif. U+03C0 GREEK SMALL LETTER PI is the one Greek letter IBM Plex Mono does have, so a maths label reading pi works in Mono while the rest of the alphabet does not."
    font-size: 7pt
    color: gray(0.3)

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Draw a checkbox with `line-style: checkbox` rather than with U+2610. It is not a font-coverage question — a drawn box is a rectangle of a stated size on a stated baseline, and a glyph is whatever the face felt like."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 60pt
  padding-top: 6pt
  gap: 12pt
  column
    width: 150pt
    box
      height: 48pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 4pt
      line-style: checkbox
      line-pitch: 7mm
      line-color: gray(0.82)
      checkbox-radius: 1pt
  column
    width: fill
    valign: middle
    text "line-style: checkbox — drawn, not set"
      font-size: 7pt
      color: gray(0.4)

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "text-transform is Unicode-aware, because it is Go's strings.ToUpper and ToLower underneath: accented Latin, Cyrillic and the IJ ligature all case-fold. The German sharp s does NOT — Go's simple case mapping has no single uppercase for it, so `straße` uppercases to STRAßE and not to STRASSE."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 74pt
  padding-top: 6pt
  gap: 10pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 58pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "straße Éclair ĳsland Ярославль"
        font-size: 8pt
    text "text-transform: none"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 58pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "straße Éclair ĳsland Ярославль"
        font-size: 8pt
        text-transform: upper
    text "text-transform: upper"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 58pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "straße Éclair ĳsland Ярославль"
        font-size: 8pt
        text-transform: lower
    text "text-transform: lower"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 58pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "straße Éclair ĳsland Ярославль"
        font-size: 8pt
        text-transform: title
    text "text-transform: title"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt

section
  height: 32pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Combining marks do NOT compose. Text is drawn glyph by glyph at its advance width with no mark positioning, so U+0301 lands beside its base letter rather than over it. Use precomposed characters."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: auto
  padding-top: 5pt
  gap: 14pt
  column
    width: 200pt
    text "precomposed: é å ü ñ"
      font-size: 13pt
  column
    width: fill
    text "combining: é å ü ñ"
      font-size: 13pt

section
  height: fill
  valign: bottom
  text "Everything on this sheet was verified by building it: the coverage table is what `treekillbot build` reported, family by family, not what the Unicode blocks suggest."
    font-size: 6.5pt
    color: gray(0.5)
